WEBVTT

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.130 --> 00:22.180
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

02:24.990 --> 02:31.990
<b>The Beginning of a Depressing and Strange Summer</b>

02:36.070 --> 02:38.840
<b>Why do you do that? {shifted forward .25}</b>

02:40.040 --> 02:42.040
<b>Because I have nothing else to do, I guess.</b>

02:44.050 --> 02:47.050
<b>Because you have nothing else to do,
 you do medical checkups on stray cats?</b>

02:48.180 --> 02:49.050
<b>Yep.</b>

02:49.050 --> 02:53.320
<b>In my spare time, I sterilize stray cats.</b>

02:53.320 --> 02:55.760
<b>But this time, it was just a medical examination.</b>

02:55.760 --> 02:57.730
<b>Those surgical procedures must be pretty tough...</b>

02:57.730 --> 03:00.500
<b>...and if you don’t get paid,
 you can’t break even, right?</b>

03:01.930 --> 03:04.730
<b>You don’t understand.
 That’s not why I do it.</b>

03:06.870 --> 03:09.770
<b>So what’ll you do, Ayumu? Going to come with me?</b>

03:12.670 --> 03:16.340
<b>I see. It did just arrive, after all.</b>

03:16.340 --> 03:17.350
<b>Umm...</b>

03:18.140 --> 03:20.610
<b>Can I head back on this?</b>

03:21.780 --> 03:23.850
<b>You want to go back to Yokohama?</b>

03:23.850 --> 03:26.080
<b>That’s not exactly what I meant, but...</b>

03:27.760 --> 03:29.550
<b>It’s up to you.</b>

03:29.550 --> 03:31.530
<b>This year sure is strange...</b>

03:33.530 --> 03:36.200
<b>Kishiro Animal Hospital</b>

03:34.300 --> 03:38.300
<b>{Animal Hospital} Even though it’s already the end of July,
 the summer camellias are still in full bloom.</b>

03:39.500 --> 03:43.570
<b>Ayumu, I respect the choices you make.</b>

03:44.870 --> 03:46.810
<b>Do what you feel is right.</b>

03:46.810 --> 03:49.510
<b>I’ll support whatever decisions you make.</b>

03:49.510 --> 03:55.480
<b>Kishiro Animal Hospital</b>

03:55.480 --> 03:58.550
<b>“This year sure is strange,” huh?</b>

04:19.540 --> 04:21.310
<b>Are you all right out there?</b>

04:21.310 --> 04:22.640
<b>What do you mean?</b>

04:22.640 --> 04:24.650
<b>Are you doing okay with that man?</b>

04:24.650 --> 04:26.720
<b>Yeah... I guess so.</b>

04:26.720 --> 04:29.680
<b>You don’t have to force yourself.
You can come back whenever you like.</b>

04:32.250 --> 04:34.920
<b>Ayumu? Are you listening to me?</b>

04:34.920 --> 04:36.360
<b>Yeah... {Tana Elementary /Kindergarten}</b>

04:36.360 --> 04:38.630
<b>This year sure is a strange one.</b>

04:38.630 --> 04:40.960
<b>For some reason, there seems to have been a lot of funerals...</b>

04:40.960 --> 04:43.270
<b>...and there’s been a huge outbreak of spiders in the garden.</b>

04:43.270 --> 04:47.970
<b>With things the way the are, I might be regretting that decision.</b>

04:47.970 --> 04:50.810
<b>Hey, I know we decided on a week...</b>

04:50.810 --> 04:53.380
<b>...but if you start to get sick of it,
just come right on home.</b>

04:53.380 --> 04:54.310
<b>Okay.</b>

04:54.310 --> 04:58.780
<b>But if I’m not here until the
mountain bike arrives, at least...</b>

04:58.780 --> 05:00.620
<b>I’ll call again.</b>

05:26.110 --> 05:28.240
<b>Ah, it’s Ayumu.</b>

05:28.240 --> 05:29.750
<b>Miku!</b>

05:35.120 --> 05:35.820
<b>Hey!</b>

05:35.820 --> 05:38.120
<b>Don’t run in the store.</b>

05:38.850 --> 05:40.350
<b>Sorry about that.</b>

05:42.920 --> 05:44.360
<b>Oh, we have a customer.</b>

05:45.090 --> 05:47.160
<b>{Farm Side Market} You should’ve called out if you were waiting.</b>

05:47.160 --> 05:49.770
<b>Mikoshiba-san’s off today, so...</b>

05:49.770 --> 05:53.070
<b>Aizawa-kun, Dr. Kishiro hasn’t come in here much since you arrived.</b>

05:53.070 --> 05:54.500
<b>Are you guys all right with food?</b>

05:54.500 --> 05:56.370
<b>I can cook, so...</b>

05:56.370 --> 05:57.770
<b>I see.</b>

05:59.240 --> 06:01.980
<b>I guess I’ve lost one of my best customers, then.</b>

06:15.660 --> 06:17.090
<b>What’s his problem?</b>

06:21.130 --> 06:22.930
<b>Aizawa Ayumu...</b>

06:22.930 --> 06:23.570
<b>...unfortunat–</b>

06:23.570 --> 06:24.370
<b>Miku.</b>

06:27.070 --> 06:29.870
<b>How do you like Tana so far?
 Not too bored?</b>

06:29.870 --> 06:32.940
<b>Well, it was as boring as it could get...</b>

06:32.940 --> 06:34.310
<b>But since this came...</b>

06:35.510 --> 06:35.980
<b>But...</b>

06:35.980 --> 06:37.480
<b>Miyama!</b>

06:37.480 --> 06:39.310
<b>Sakakura.</b>

06:41.250 --> 06:42.780
<b>I thought I saw you when I looked back.</b>

06:42.780 --> 06:45.650
<b>And it really was you.</b>

06:45.650 --> 06:46.290
<b>Who’s that?</b>

06:47.560 --> 06:49.060
<b>Aizawa-kun.</b>

06:49.060 --> 06:51.060
<b>You know, the son of Dr. Kishiro.</b>

06:51.060 --> 06:53.800
<b>Huh? But aren’t their last names different?</b>

06:53.800 --> 06:56.600
<b>This is why you’re useless.</b>

06:56.600 --> 06:59.070
<b>These things called “family issues”
 exist, you know.</b>

07:00.440 --> 07:03.570
<b>Sorry, but I’ll pass on any complicated stories. {That’s a pretty cool story, but I’ll have to pass.}</b>

07:03.570 --> 07:04.970
<b>Anyway, Miyama...</b>

07:05.810 --> 07:08.110
<b>Have you heard about Old Lady Okaka?</b>

07:08.110 --> 07:09.540
<b>Didn’t she die?</b>

07:09.540 --> 07:11.280
<b>Apparently she’s been reborn!</b>

07:11.280 --> 07:13.010
<b>Huh? Seriously?</b>

07:13.010 --> 07:15.220
<b>She could be a ghost!</b>

07:15.220 --> 07:18.790
<b>Rather... wouldn’t it mean that she never actually died?</b>

07:18.790 --> 07:20.490
<b>Aizawa Ayumu.</b>

07:20.490 --> 07:23.490
<b>Do you know who Old Lady Okaka is?
 She’s a cat.</b>

07:23.490 --> 07:26.800
<b>The rival of Sakakura, from ten years ago.</b>

07:26.800 --> 07:27.830
<b>A cat?</b>

07:27.830 --> 07:28.460
<b>Yeah.</b>

07:28.460 --> 07:30.270
<b>Don’t make fun of me!</b>

07:30.270 --> 07:33.240
<b>No, it’s just... I don’t really understand...</b>

07:33.240 --> 07:34.940
<b>She’s not just some normal tortoiseshell cat. {?}</b>

07:34.940 --> 07:36.610
<b>And there’s no way she’s a stray.</b>

07:36.610 --> 07:38.470
<b>Sometimes I doubt whether she’s really even a cat!</b>

07:38.470 --> 07:39.610
<b>There he goes, starting up on that again...</b>

07:39.610 --> 07:41.980
<b>She got her ear torn off fighting a kappa!</b>

07:41.980 --> 07:44.950
<b>A tortoiseshell cat with one ear torn off? I saw it.</b>

07:44.950 --> 07:46.480
<b>“I”?</b>

07:47.050 --> 07:50.250
<b>All right, Mr. “I,”{note on this?} where did you see her?</b>

07:51.450 --> 07:52.990
<b>In the garden at my Dad’s place.</b>

07:52.990 --> 07:54.560
<b>The vet, huh?</b>

07:59.730 --> 08:01.230
<b>Sometimes I wonder about him...</b>

08:01.230 --> 08:03.070
<b>That thing about it fighting with a kappa...</b>

08:03.070 --> 08:06.230
<b>Sakakura says he saw it when he was in elementary school...</b>

08:06.230 --> 08:09.170
<b>Old Lady Okaka and a kappa battling... {inv}</b>

08:10.170 --> 08:11.870
<b>I have no reaction for that.</b>

08:11.870 --> 08:14.710
<b>Kappas do exist.
They’re further up the river.</b>

08:14.710 --> 08:17.150
<b>Now that I think about it,{s}</b>

08:17.150 --> 08:20.920
<b>Mikoshiba-san did say the fireflies
 were increasing up the Nakizawagawa River.</b>

08:20.920 --> 08:23.690
<b>And that there was something else there, too...</b>

08:23.690 --> 08:28.460
<b>Yeah. There’s also the 
ghost stories of Emerald Land.</b>

08:28.460 --> 08:31.660
<b>This year might be a little stranger than last.</b>

08:34.030 --> 08:41.500
<b>Kishiro Animal Hospital</b>

08:44.840 --> 08:46.480
<b>Damn. She got away, huh?</b>

08:53.440 --> 08:55.150
<b>Secondary River Channel</b>

09:21.740 --> 09:23.650
<b>Hello.</b>

09:23.650 --> 09:26.110
<b>Do you have business at 
my Tsukiyomi Observatory?</b>

09:26.110 --> 09:27.020
<b>N-No...</b>

09:28.250 --> 09:31.090
<b>This is the Tsukiyomi Observatory, in which you learn about the night.</b>

09:33.720 --> 09:36.460
<b>The time of the supernatural will come when the boundary opens.</b>

09:36.460 --> 09:38.790
<b>This world’s membrane grows thinner by the day.</b>

09:38.790 --> 09:42.760
<b>If you’re heading into the mountains, be careful.</b>

10:26.040 --> 10:27.910
<b>That must’ve been Heigorou-san.</b>

10:27.910 --> 10:30.610
<b>Of the so-called “Tsukiyomi Observatory.”</b>

10:30.610 --> 10:33.320
<b>I hate to say this,
 but this isn’t all that good...</b>

10:34.380 --> 10:36.990
<b>Would you have preferred 
my home-made boxed meal?</b>

10:36.990 --> 10:39.890
<b>No... that’s not the problem here...</b>

10:40.620 --> 10:42.490
<b>I’ll cook, so...</b>

10:42.490 --> 10:46.230
<b>Sorry for not contacting you, but you don’t have to buy these things anymore.</b>

10:48.230 --> 10:49.460
<b>What kind of person is he?</b>

10:50.630 --> 10:51.870
<b>Heigorou-san. {rw}</b>

10:51.870 --> 10:52.970
<b>I’m not too sure myself.</b>

10:52.970 --> 10:54.800
<b>There are lots of rumors about him, though.</b>

10:54.800 --> 10:58.510
<b>It’s like... all the people around here are kind of weird, huh?</b>

10:58.510 --> 10:59.880
<b>You think so?</b>

11:00.840 --> 11:02.410
<b>It feels like everyone’s being pushed away from something...</b>

11:02.410 --> 11:03.350
<b>From what?</b>

11:03.350 --> 11:04.810
<b>Common sense.</b>

11:04.810 --> 11:08.020
<b>Isn’t that rather healthy?</b>

11:08.020 --> 11:09.580
<b>Really? Why?</b>

11:09.580 --> 11:12.990
<b>Well... I can’t really explain it...</b>

11:14.060 --> 11:16.020
<b>You’re forcing yourself to say that.</b>

11:16.020 --> 11:18.190
<b>Am not. I’m just being flexible.</b>

11:18.890 --> 11:20.200
<b>Acting this way doesn’t suit you.</b>

11:20.200 --> 11:21.300
<b>You think so?</b>

11:21.300 --> 11:23.170
<b>Well then, how come you can’t explain it?</b>

11:23.170 --> 11:24.570
<b>Well...</b>

11:24.570 --> 11:26.540
<b>In the first place, “common sense” is...</b>

11:26.540 --> 11:29.440
<b>...nothing more than taking the lowest common denominator from where you are at the time.</b>

11:29.440 --> 11:30.470
<b>Thanks for the food.</b>

11:30.470 --> 11:33.760
<b>I mean, it’s fine for people who don’t have to ingratiate themselves to others{s}</b>

11:33.760 --> 11:35.540
<b>to go at their own pace.</b>

11:35.540 --> 11:36.850
<b>Is that really all right?</b>

11:36.850 --> 11:38.450
<b>Is it okay to leave people like that alone?</b>

11:38.450 --> 11:40.620
<b>Is there a reason not to?</b>

11:40.620 --> 11:44.490
<b>Well, I suppose people who lack common sense might tend to be anti-social...</b>

11:44.490 --> 11:49.360
<b>...and that’s the part where I think things get hard to explain.</b>

11:49.360 --> 11:52.430
<b>But it must be tough if they don’t ingratiate themselves to the people they’re with.</b>

11:52.430 --> 11:55.430
<b>Just ingratiating yourself to the people you meet is pretty tough, too.</b>

11:56.900 --> 12:00.100
<b>Everything depends on what the person chooses.</b>

12:00.100 --> 12:04.840
<b>And in general, shouldn’t the way a person lives be decided by themselves and not by others?</b>

12:16.780 --> 12:19.250
<b>The mountain bike arrived today.</b>

12:21.850 --> 12:24.850
<b>The mountain bike arrived today.
I’m going to stay here a little bit longer.</b>

12:25.120 --> 12:26.830
<b>Sending</b>

13:03.690 --> 13:05.310
<b>Hey, Mr. “I.”</b>

13:05.310 --> 13:07.720
<b>Have you seen Old Lady Okaka 
since yesterday?</b>

13:07.720 --> 13:09.480
<b>Nope.</b>

13:09.480 --> 13:11.750
<b>I guess she’s up in EmeLan then, huh?</b>

13:16.630 --> 13:18.110
<b>Here’s the newspaper.</b>

13:19.030 --> 13:20.730
<b>This sure feels weird...</b>

13:20.730 --> 13:21.830
<b>What does?</b>

13:21.830 --> 13:23.830
<b>No, it’s nothing...</b>

13:23.830 --> 13:25.670
<b>Quit stopping in the middle
 of your sentences.</b>

13:25.670 --> 13:27.100
<b>It’s creepy.</b>

13:29.200 --> 13:31.860
<b>This miso soup...
It tastes the same as Junko’s...</b>

13:33.610 --> 13:35.830
<b>...as your mother’s used to.</b>

13:35.830 --> 13:37.710
<b>It’s because she drilled it into me.</b>

13:37.710 --> 13:38.710
<b>I see.</b>

13:41.150 --> 13:42.800
<b>EmeLan...</b>

13:42.800 --> 13:45.320
<b>What was it... Emerald Land, I think?</b>

13:45.320 --> 13:46.620
<b>What kind of place is it?</b>

13:46.620 --> 13:48.020
<b>A resort.</b>

13:48.020 --> 13:50.410
<b>A resort? In a town like this?</b>

13:50.410 --> 13:52.990
<b>It’s because you can see Mt. Fuji from up there.</b>

13:54.330 --> 13:59.070
<b>But you know... a lot of people abandon their pets up there, so it’s a problem.</b>

13:59.070 --> 14:01.040
<b>They come to the resort with their pet...</b>

14:01.040 --> 14:03.870
<b>...and for some reason, their animals are left behind when they leave.</b>

14:03.870 --> 14:06.360
<b>So that’s why you give those stray cats medical examinations?</b>

14:07.980 --> 14:11.900
<b>How long do you think an average stray cat lives?</b>

14:13.860 --> 14:16.170
<b>Ten years, maybe?</b>

14:16.170 --> 14:18.690
<b>Pet cats live more than a decade.</b>

14:18.690 --> 14:21.860
<b>These days, it’s not unusual for pet cats
to live for twenty years. {Today, a pet cat living to the age of twenty isn’t all that unusual.}</b>

14:21.860 --> 14:26.180
<b>But stray cats normally live an average of two years.</b>

14:26.180 --> 14:27.400
<b>But that’s just the average, right?</b>

14:27.400 --> 14:30.700
<b>If that were the case, shouldn’t there be a lot of kittens around here?</b>

14:30.700 --> 14:31.920
<b>Well, there’s that point, too.</b>

14:31.920 --> 14:34.140
<b>However, the number of cats will pretty much stay the same,{s}</b>

14:34.140 --> 14:36.270
<b>even if their breeds are different.{rc}</b>

14:36.270 --> 14:41.280
<b>To put it simply, I think many of the cats just can’t make it through the winter.</b>

14:41.280 --> 14:42.880
<b>Sure sounds difficult.</b>

14:42.880 --> 14:44.750
<b>Don’t summarize it so easily.</b>

14:44.750 --> 14:45.630
<b>Okay.</b>

14:49.850 --> 14:52.070
<b>You can’t ever abandon what you think is right.</b>

14:52.690 --> 14:54.020
<b>Understand?</b>

14:54.020 --> 14:55.040
<b>Yeah.</b>

15:33.440 --> 15:36.800
<b>I left your lunch in the microwave.</b>

15:56.400 --> 15:58.400
<b>Kamikaze</b>

15:56.400 --> 15:58.400
<b> Cat Dance</b>

16:20.780 --> 16:21.910
<b>Ayumu.</b>

16:24.180 --> 16:26.380
<b>Are you going to see the kappa?</b>

16:26.380 --> 16:28.350
<b>No.</b>

16:28.350 --> 16:29.850
<b>Oh, I see!</b>

16:29.850 --> 16:32.070
<b>Then you’re going to see Wakkun, 
aren’t you?</b>

16:32.070 --> 16:34.520
<b>Huh? Who’s that?</b>

16:40.360 --> 16:42.030
<b>Wakkun’s gonna cry!</b>

16:42.030 --> 16:44.470
<b>Also, it’s gonna rain tonight.</b>

16:44.470 --> 16:46.450
<b>Right, right.</b>

16:49.910 --> 16:50.710
<b>Hey...</b>

16:59.450 --> 17:01.100
<b>Ignoring me again?!</b>

17:07.320 --> 17:08.810
<b>Weird...</b>

17:31.250 --> 17:32.430
<b>Let me take shelter here.</b>

17:32.430 --> 17:34.020
<b>Sure.</b>

17:34.020 --> 17:36.180
<b>As long as you buy something.</b>

17:36.180 --> 17:39.470
<b>Also, loitering near the magazines while wet is prohibited.</b>

17:39.470 --> 17:40.600
<b>Yes, ma’am.</b>

17:52.130 --> 17:53.850
<b><i>What am I doing...?</i></b>

17:53.850 --> 17:56.640
<b><i>Or rather... what do I want to do?</i></b>

17:57.820 --> 18:00.110
<b>Thank you very much!</b>

18:01.580 --> 18:02.540
<b>My...</b>

18:03.810 --> 18:05.310
<b>It’s just a passing rainstorm.</b>

18:05.310 --> 18:07.320
<b>I think it’ll let up soon.</b>

18:10.770 --> 18:13.740
<b>Old Lady</b>

18:10.770 --> 18:13.740
<b>Okaka</b>

18:10.770 --> 18:12.170
<b>Tacchan</b>

18:11.870 --> 18:13.740
<b>Tacchan</b>

18:21.560 --> 18:22.700
<b>Hello?</b>

18:24.180 --> 18:28.150
<b>Kishiro Animal Hospital</b>

18:34.140 --> 18:36.090
<b>Leave me alone, Papa!</b>

18:36.090 --> 18:38.050
<b>I don’t wanna talk about it anymore!</b>

19:09.460 --> 19:11.100
<b>Taku</b>

19:11.100 --> 19:11.220
<b>Taku</b>

19:11.230 --> 19:11.360
<b>Taku</b>

19:11.360 --> 19:11.590
<b>Taku</b>

19:11.600 --> 19:11.730
<b>Taku</b>

19:11.730 --> 19:11.860
<b>Taku</b>

19:11.860 --> 19:11.960
<b>Taku</b>

19:11.960 --> 19:12.460
<b>Taku</b>

19:12.460 --> 19:13.930
<b>Taku</b>

19:12.460 --> 19:13.930
<b>Dialing</b>

20:06.500 --> 20:07.840
<b>Could you be...</b>

20:09.950 --> 20:11.540
<b>Wakkun?</b>

20:26.220 --> 20:27.360
<b>Are you all right?</b>

20:27.920 --> 20:28.840
<b>You came.</b>

20:29.960 --> 20:31.430
<b>I was waiting for you.</b>

20:31.430 --> 20:33.300
<b>Um... I don’t understand.</b>

20:33.300 --> 20:37.270
<b>And anyway... what are you doing here all by yourself?</b>

20:37.270 --> 20:38.530
<b>Playing.</b>

20:38.530 --> 20:39.640
<b>Playing what?</b>

20:39.640 --> 20:41.290
<b>Playing to play.</b>

20:45.740 --> 20:47.080
<b>Come with me for a sec!</b>

20:50.280 --> 20:52.710
<b>Playing here at this hour...</b>

20:52.710 --> 20:54.720
<b>Your family must be worried sick. {inv}</b>

20:54.720 --> 20:56.250
<b>I don’t have one.</b>

20:56.250 --> 20:58.290
<b>I have the Shinies. {was this term changed in later eps?}</b>

20:58.290 --> 21:00.420
<b>Umm... I have to...</b>

21:00.420 --> 21:01.620
<b>Look, look!</b>

21:04.630 --> 21:05.760
<b>This is...</b>

21:05.760 --> 21:06.680
<b>The Shinies!</b>

21:08.930 --> 21:10.730
<b>We can play again, right?</b>

21:14.970 --> 21:15.840
<b>No?</b>

21:17.170 --> 21:19.170
<b>Please play with me again.</b>

21:19.840 --> 21:21.660
<b>O-Okay...</b>

21:22.780 --> 21:23.910
<b>Thanks.</b>

21:44.070 --> 21:48.050
<b>Roku, there’s nothing there. Don’t worry about it.</b>

21:48.050 --> 21:50.770
<b>Umm... these aren’t fireflies, are they?</b>

21:50.770 --> 21:51.870
<b>What are they?</b>

21:51.870 --> 21:53.010
<b>Shinies.</b>

21:53.010 --> 21:53.780
<b>Like I said...</b>

21:53.780 --> 21:55.610
<b>Just look at them.</b>

21:55.610 --> 21:57.510
<b>Umm, I am, but...</b>

22:08.220 --> 22:09.730
<b>See, see?</b>

22:09.730 --> 22:11.740
<b>Shinies...?</b>

22:12.860 --> 22:14.860
<b>Let’s play together again.</b>

22:15.460 --> 22:17.170
<b>I’ll be waiting for you...</b>

22:24.170 --> 22:25.340
<b>Hey...</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

24:19.970 --> 24:22.660
<b>Hi there! I’m the Chihuahua, Taruto!</b>

24:19.970 --> 24:22.970
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

24:22.660 --> 24:24.630
<b>I’m a lively seventeen months old!</b>

24:24.630 --> 24:27.480
<b>I call my owner Shione “Nene-chan”!</b>

24:27.480 --> 24:29.500
<b>Hmph. I’m Old Lady Okaka.</b>

24:29.500 --> 24:33.050
<b>Geez, grandma! This is your self-introduction,
but you show no grace!</b>

24:33.050 --> 24:36.680
<b>Good day. I’m Roku. I live with Heigorou-san
at the Tsukiyomi Observatory.</b>

24:36.680 --> 24:38.880
<b>I belong to the Labrador Retriever family of dogs.</b>

24:38.880 --> 24:40.320
<b>He sure is formal.</b>

24:40.320 --> 24:42.580
<b>Yeah, Rokkun. You need to go with the flow.</b>

24:42.580 --> 24:44.760
<b>Next time, you might be the main character, too!</b>

24:44.760 --> 24:46.290
<b>Really? Okay!</b>

24:46.290 --> 24:47.190
<b>Sorry to keep you waiting!</b>

24:47.190 --> 24:50.260
<b>I’m Roku, and I live with Mr. Heigorou
at his chateau! Nice to meet you!</b>

24:50.260 --> 24:51.770
<b>He’s just not good at this stuff.</b>

24:51.770 --> 24:54.530
<b>Next time: “The Tsukiyomi Observatory
and Old Lady Okaka.”</b>

24:54.530 --> 24:56.870
<b>Huh? Didn’t you just say Old Lady Okaka?</b>

24:55.000 --> 24:59.950
<b>The Tsukiyomi Observatory
and Old Lady Okaka</b>

24:56.870 --> 24:58.070
<b>You did, didn’t you?</b>
